## 4. Agent-Native Automation Layer (MCP)

Fixed pipelines do one sequence well, but every new capability costs as much as the last one and nothing is reusable. This layer puts the capabilities behind a Model Context Protocol server as composable skills.

- **Skill registry.** Each capability is a self-contained module with a name, description, input schema, and run function. It is discovered automatically and callable from a CLI or an MCP client with no extra wiring.
- **Read-only by default.** Every skill shipped so far is read-only. Writing to production records requires a deliberate design decision, explicit safeguards, and approval.
- **Protocol hygiene.** Diagnostic output goes to stderr so it doesn't corrupt the JSON-RPC stream. Blocking work runs off the async event loop.
- **Inspectable results.** Every tool returns structured output that records which strategy succeeded.

**Stack:** Python · Playwright · MCP (FastMCP) · anyio

